# Open Laws India — Licensing Information

The `kanoonhq/open-laws` project employs a dual-licensing structure to guarantee unrestricted public and commercial access:

---

## 1. Statutory Data, Footnotes & Mappings: CC0 1.0 Universal (Public Domain Dedication)

To the extent possible under law, KanoonHQ has waived all copyright and related or neighboring rights to the statutory text, bare acts, sections, legislative amendment footnotes, and transition crosswalk mappings contained in this repository.

This work is published from: **India**.

### Statutory Exemption under Indian Law
Under **Section 52(1)(q) of the Indian Copyright Act, 1957**, the reproduction or publication of:
- (i) any matter which has been published in any Official Gazette;
- (ii) any Act of a Legislature;
- (iii) any report of any committee, commission, council, board or other like body appointed by the Government;
- (iv) any judgment, order or decree of a court, tribunal or other judicial authority;
**does not constitute an infringement of copyright**.

The raw statutory law belongs unconditionally to the public domain.

For the full legal code of CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

